    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, from the code as it currently stands. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:162`).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (runs before the method body)\n\nApplied to `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Valid`; failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`\n3. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n4. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n5. `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n6. `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)` each\n7. `email` \u2014 `@Size(3..255)`, `@Email`\n\nNo custom validators, `@InitBinder`, or Spring `Validator` apply to this endpoint (the only custom constraint, `@PetAgeValidation`, is for pets).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Controller body, in execution order\n\n8. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before (static in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`), re-fetch that owner and return **200** (skips everything below).\n9. **`rejectMissingOrBlankFields`** \u2014 manual blank checks on `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and requires at least one of `addressLine1`/`address` \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400).\n10. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (MapStruct; `id`/`pets` ignored).\n11. **`applyAddress`** *(side-effect: mutates entity)* \u2014 normalizes/upper-cases address, collapses whitespace, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n12. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 strips separators, forces E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops leading `0`), enforces per-country digit length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n13. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 trims, validates pattern (`InvalidEmailException`, 400), lower-cases, rejects disposable domains mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail (`DisposableEmailDomainException`, 400).\n14. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW/VIC/QLD) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n15. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 supplied date > today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n16. **Default registrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if null, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n17. **`rollToBusinessDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 rolls weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day.\n18. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 \u2265100 owners with same registrationDate \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n19. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 \u226550 owners in same city \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` (**409**).\n20. **`computeHouseholdId`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode`.\n21. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 exact match on `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n22. **`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`** \u2014 only when `sharesHousehold` is false; any owner with same `householdId` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n23. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when last name + postcode match but phone differs.\n24. **`generateCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `REGION-HASH8` from SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName`, de-duplicated with `-n` suffix.\n25. **`countNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount`.\n26. **`countHouseholdSize`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` (existing + 1).\n27. **`isBulkSignupDay`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` if >80 owners already on that date.\n28. **PERSIST** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 JPA `save`/`persist` (`@Transactional`). DB assigns the identity id.\n29. **Record idempotency** *(side-effect)* \u2014 store the new id under the `Idempotency-Key` in the static map.\n30. **Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** \u2014 computes read-time derived fields (displayName, initials, membership number/points/level, Luhn check digit, etc.); not persisted.\n31. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT` logger emits `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 \u2026`.\n32. **Set `Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Persistence-layer / entity-level side-effects\n\n33. **Entity Bean Validation on flush** (Hibernate): `Owner.address @NotEmpty`, `city @NotEmpty`, `telephone @NotEmpty @Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`; `Person.firstName/lastName @NotEmpty` \u2192 `ConstraintViolationException` on commit.\n34. **DB constraints** (`schema.sql`): NOT-NULL and length caps on the owners columns; only a **non-unique** `idx_owners_last_name` index \u2014 uniqueness is enforced by the in-code checks (steps 21\u201322), not the DB. A DB violation \u2192 `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 **404**.\n35. `pets` cascade is `ALL` but empty on create, so **no cascade persists**. There are **no** `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`, entity listeners, or JPA auditing.\n\n## Things that look relevant but do NOT run\n\n- **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** is **not enforced** by default: `petclinic.security.enable=false`, and `@EnableMethodSecurity` lives only in the disabled security config.\n- **`CallMonitoringAspect`** is never registered as a bean (no `@Component`), so it does not execute.\n- No filters, `HandlerInterceptor`s, `WebMvcConfigurer`s, emails/notifications, published events, password encoding, or external service calls are involved.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: nearly every step from 18 onward performs its own full-table `findAllOwners()` read, so a single create triggers many full scans of the owners table."
